{"id": "EUVD-2026-58880", "enisaUuid": "108b9e5e-4f7e-364e-8312-5ea6e03738be", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncan: bcm: fix lockless bound/ifindex race and silent RX_SETUP failure\n\nbcm_sendmsg() reads bo->ifindex and checks bo->bound before taking\nlock_sock(), while bcm_notify(), bcm_connect() and bcm_release() all\nmutate both fields under that same lock. Because the lockless reads\nand the locked writes are unordered with respect to each other, a\nracing bcm_notify() (device unregister) or bcm_connect() (concurrent\nbind on another thread sharing the socket) can make bcm_sendmsg()\nobserve an inconsistent combination, e.g. a stale bound=1 together\nwith the now-cleared ifindex=0, silently turning a socket bound to a\nspecific CAN interface into one that also matches \"any\" interface.\n\nKeep the lockless bo->bound check purely as a fast-path reject, and\nmove the ifindex read (and a bo->bound re-check) into the locked\nsection, where every writer already serializes. This removes the\npossibility of observing the two fields torn against each other,\nrather than trying to fix it with more READ_ONCE()/WRITE_ONCE() pairs\non two independently updated fields. Annotate the now-purely-lockless\nbo->bound accesses consistently across all its write sites.\n\nAlso fix bcm_rx_setup() silently returning success when the target\ndevice disappears concurrently instead of reporting -ENODEV, so a\nbroken RX op is no longer left registered as if it had succeeded.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:53:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:44:57", "baseScore": 7.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:L", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9e60c586faeaed80d55ab8ce2a4b8e56133bc395", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ffa80a2af27c97453861a5128e537214a31cd18a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6bcc5cd247c2934373bc2a1cdf8bf12321169543", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f6f9f95294b4cbb26ba02209e893e3bd91237c3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b70f1a15533afeeec5d07f20bec3f3867ab1c7b6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/35f0ac19efb1a3f6c5e12c00e475a9ec2d9c3a6d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b9c6ac6fb4e01b34575816066e5d3890a57b3c86", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d9b091d9d22fee81ec53fb55d2032951993ceadb"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4cqx-6pr4-c34w", "CVE-2026-72122"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01c9b423-abe2-30ce-a275-dc868f722a1d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ffd980f976e7fd666c2e61bf8ab35107efd11828 <b70f1a15533afeeec5d07f20bec3f3867ab1c7b6"}, {"id": "097cb465-e879-348a-a16c-be644dfdf765", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ffd980f976e7fd666c2e61bf8ab35107efd11828 <ffa80a2af27c97453861a5128e537214a31cd18a"}, {"id": "1ae99072-00b7-3776-95c3-6a149952c818", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.178"}, {"id": "32e73280-f9b5-3a7a-963a-0e387ba46438", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "36a735f4-0cb9-3ebf-a2da-5392c5d99e5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.212"}, {"id": "4186f249-4a6f-3fe5-a524-b86a8a87b72a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ffd980f976e7fd666c2e61bf8ab35107efd11828 <d9b091d9d22fee81ec53fb55d2032951993ceadb"}, {"id": "44698bed-3138-35d0-bbd1-0d6437757839", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "63a1c440-4075-3577-9d44-49fc113cf794", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ffd980f976e7fd666c2e61bf8ab35107efd11828 <0f6f9f95294b4cbb26ba02209e893e3bd91237c3"}, {"id": "74ecabef-2ca0-37da-9a75-7f2aa9d3fe54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.25"}, {"id": "7d0b9a86-3326-33a3-895b-4b99f038f7f4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.261"}, {"id": "83f71eeb-e3d6-3829-baa0-8b79a6d0a4cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "8e615d09-0179-3ea4-988a-068753ccbfb4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ffd980f976e7fd666c2e61bf8ab35107efd11828 <6bcc5cd247c2934373bc2a1cdf8bf12321169543"}, {"id": "acc7e165-c281-32c5-af1f-903f4be09ab0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b5a9fc64-1641-3512-bc62-06dbee3d3d58", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "b6ea5a89-831f-349b-af19-a8e3eab693a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ffd980f976e7fd666c2e61bf8ab35107efd11828 <35f0ac19efb1a3f6c5e12c00e475a9ec2d9c3a6d"}, {"id": "cf7420b0-06d6-3d17-8061-d48916dad3fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "e78f2cc9-b67e-3244-ae3c-c00387a6803d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ffd980f976e7fd666c2e61bf8ab35107efd11828 <9e60c586faeaed80d55ab8ce2a4b8e56133bc395"}, {"id": "ef818489-5949-34fd-b689-dfd0c5921025", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ffd980f976e7fd666c2e61bf8ab35107efd11828 <b9c6ac6fb4e01b34575816066e5d3890a57b3c86"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bfcfc95f-8e0a-3b98-bd84-aa53c24007ae", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}